# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Giulio Benedini et al. (2025). Universal machine learning potentials for systems with reduced dimensionality.
#   AI for Science. doi:10.1088/3050-287x/ae1208  arXiv:2508.15614v1
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2508.15614v1 (sha256 ff537f7aa37f4454...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 392 (Application/model instance). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/benedini2025.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: the 0123D data set (40,000 PBE-relaxed compounds,
# 10,000 each of 0D, 1D, 2D and 3D, built outside existing training sets
# and the WBM set; Alexandria settings) and the 11 pretrained universal
# MLIPs of Table I evaluated on it as distributed (geometry
# optimisation). Energy errors (Fig. 5), position errors (Fig. 6) and
# convergence failures (Table II) are figure-only or counts; the text
# gives only qualitative ranges, so no metrics are encoded.

@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
